---
functions:
  command:
  - blind: true
    code: |-
      echo /path/to/command | batch
    comment: |-
      The command is executed when the system load average drops below 1.5 (or the value specified by [atd](../atd)).
    contexts:
      sudo:
      unprivileged:
  shell:
  - code: |-
      echo "/bin/sh <$(tty) >$(tty) 2>$(tty)" | batch; tail -f /dev/null
    comment: |-
      `tail` is used to pause the terminal. The shell starts when the system load average drops below 1.5.
    contexts:
      sudo:
      unprivileged:
...
